      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZONKSTAR (2) won on debut over 1400m but looked as though he already wanted this distance last start on the Illawarra Grange circuit. An inside draw with Boudvillain booked is a big push for his chances and he lands here with plenty of upside. Can bounce back to winning ways. TOUSSAINT (4) is the main danger if forgiven for the BM68 failure at Kembla Grange, where she was bumped and beaten a long way after starting near the top of an open market; her prior Goulburn win as favourite keeps her right in play. MIDNIGHT AFFAIR (3) drops out of BM74 grade and steps out to this trip for the first time. Wouldn't surprise to see it suit and she can make an impression. THAT A BOY (5) was close enough at Wagga and not far from TOUSSAINT two back. Not out of this on recent form. MAGIC MOUNTAIN (8) is better than he showed last time out and won't be far away.",
